{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790758504,"nonce":"NvV04VbfFp1dp/6GWQ1Jh1Bg29s=","title":"Coerce nullable start indexes at String wrapper calls","message":"Issue4729 passes a nullable Int from an inline local function to String.indexOf. The value prints as 6, but the native wrapper receives a pointer-shaped argument where its third parameter is a plain Int; searching for a space after index 6 returns -1 rather than 11. The same mismatch applies to String.lastIndexOf with an explicit nullable start index.\n\nThe extern-class MIR wrapper call now coerces a pointer-shaped start index for the two String search overloads to Int before the call. Direct integer start indexes retain their existing path. An authored regression covers indexOf, lastIndexOf, and the inline local function pattern.\n\nIn an isolated build with only the fix applied, Issue4729 changed WRONG_ANSWER to PASS (2 assertions), TestArrowFunctions stayed PASS (10 assertions), and all 98 authored regressions passed. The full tiered run scored 786/1094; Issue4729 improved while known-flaky Issue10083 reversed a pass from the previous run. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.","files":null}]}